WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.120
Okay, I need to talk to you about something
that's really important today and I need some

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.569
time to lay this all out for you, but hope

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:07.569
it'll be productive.

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:13.759
Yesterday I started getting emails and seeing
comments saying, David, will you disclose

00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:20.350
your funding and will you disclose whether
you're getting money from a pro Bashar Al

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:27.269
Assad group that is in existence to prop up
the Syrian regime, disclose your funding and

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:28.760
tell us who your funders are.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.980
And it seemed like a weird thing to ask of
me.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.080
I didn't understand why are people coming
to me and saying, am I getting funding from

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.910
a, from a pro Bashar Al Assad group?

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.120
So I started researching this and then I saw
a couple of reports and posts that there are

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.600
several left wing independent media people
that have allegedly received money from a

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.340
pro Assad group, some under the guise of a
journalism award, money that was awarded a

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.620
for winning a journalism a prize.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.500
So I want to do this and I'm going to give
you the full breakdown of our revenue at the

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.500
end of the segment.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.410
But let's go through this and actually try
to do it right.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.680
So let's begin with what are the allegations?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:11.240
The allegations are that several left wing
independent media hosts and writers and publications

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.920
received money from a group called the association
for investment in popular action committees.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.050
It's a very sort of innocuous name, uh, but
investigative reporting by Charles David,

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:28.250
uh, claims to demonstrate that this is actually
an umbrella organization that is a covering

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:35.790
for and the sort of a, a name place holder
for a, uh, groups that are pro Syrian dictator

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.120
Bashar Al Assad.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.630
The association for investment in popular
action committees has a trademark called the

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:47.760
serious solidarity movement, which again,
it sounds pro rights, but it's, it's pro Assad.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.320
And the idea here is that this is an umbrella
group for pro Syrian government organizations.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.050
When you look at them on GuideStar, it's very
innocuous.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.570
It's a civil rights advocacy group organized
in 2007.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.190
There's limited information.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:06.460
It's headed up by two guys, Paul LA, Rudy
and Kemal obeyed.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.830
And when I started looking into this, and
this is all new to me, I've, you know, I did,

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:15.520
did the research over the last 24 hours, obeyed
has said that he was a member of architects

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.100
and engineers for nine 11 truth, which is
a nine 11 truther group.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.770
I would call it a conspiracy group.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.390
So it's starting to get a little bit weird.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.940
And the revelations that have come forward
for independent media are that this group

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:36.060
has created something called the Serena Shem
award for uncompromised integrity in journalism,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.150
which awards money to different media people.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.849
They've paid former Ohio governor, a democratic
governor, Dennis QSEN.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:48.050
It's $20,000 to speak at a proba Shar al-Assad
conference in the United Kingdom.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:54.050
And, um, it's so happened that Cousineau synNotch,
uh, opted not to condemn Assad a few years

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:55.050
ago.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:00.600
And it turns out that some people, including
former TYT host Jimmy Dora, Dory, I don't

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.290
know how the name is pronounced now, as well
as YouTube or Kim Iverson, who I didn't know

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:10.940
much about, and many others have received
money from this group through this award.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.130
Now let's go, go through it.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.670
Uh, there are some trends that exist here.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:22.349
Both DOR and Iverson have done a combination
of questioning the known facts about Bashar

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:28.690
Al Assad and have started to dabble in some
conspiratorial false flag stuff as well.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:35.330
Both DOR and Iverson have put out content
that is very pro Tulsi Gabbert and Tulsi has

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.060
her own sort of history with Assad.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.920
That has been the subject of scrutiny.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:45.270
There is an IRS filing, which you can easily
find online, uh, from the pro Assad group,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:50.690
which shows that in 2017 DOR receive $2,500
from this group while Kim Iverson previously

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:55.319
posted to Instagram that she received $5,000
from the group.

00:03:55.319 --> 00:03:58.569
So the first question is, can we trust the
allegation?

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:02.560
In other words, did these people and the others
that are listed in the piece that we're linking

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.500
to, did they receive this money?

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.610
Iverson admits she got the money, she posted
about it.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.440
And unless the IRS filings are false, DOR
did as well.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.310
There's a longer list of people you can find
online, but the part one, did they get the

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.310
money?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.310
It appears that they did.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.280
So then we have to ask, well, even if it's
a pro Assad group that is funding the award,

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:28.789
uh, are they, is, are they getting money to
say certain things or are they merely being

00:04:28.789 --> 00:04:31.300
awarded for the things that they're already
choosing to say?

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.009
And I think that this is an important distinction
with a lot.

00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:35.110
We've talked about this before.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:39.259
You know, that it's common that people at
Fox news, people at RT, Russian television,

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:43.360
they'll say, nobody ever comes in and tells
me exactly what I need to say.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.509
And of course it doesn't work that way.

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:47.740
It's not say this stuff and then we will pay
you.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.400
It is often that people are selected for roles
on the basis of what they're already likely

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.400
to say.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.080
So we really don't know the, the, the reality
of this.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.080
That's one thing.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.689
Uh, then there's this issue, you know, it,
it correlates with the pro Tulsi stuff and

00:05:01.689 --> 00:05:05.439
alternative facts around Syria and related
topics.

00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:08.099
This is odd, but ultimately it's their business.

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:11.499
Now, if it were me, I would disclose this
stuff full-stop.

00:05:11.499 --> 00:05:14.569
I mean, I don't, I don't have any other way
that I would qualify it.

00:05:14.569 --> 00:05:16.330
I would just disclose it.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.150
So then we come to me in the emails I've been
getting over the last 14, 16 hours saying,

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:24.250
David, you're part of this, disclose your
funding.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.719
We want to know where you get your money.

00:05:25.719 --> 00:05:27.310
So I'm going to do that.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:31.159
First of all, I don't know why anyone would
think I'm getting money from a pro Assad group

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:36.360
or pro Assad sources, uh, particularly that
are peddling and you know, uh, were their

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.979
leaders, uh, the, this obeyed guy pedals in
nine 11 truth or stuff or anything?

00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:41.330
I don't do any of what they do.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.930
You know, I, I don't do Assad apologetics.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.349
I don't do pro Tulsi apologetics.

00:05:46.349 --> 00:05:47.930
I don't do any of this stuff.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.560
But I'll just come clean and tell you our
funding.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.740
This is from a normal month.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:55.080
This is data from August the [inaudible],
it's the beginning of October.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.729
So I haven't closed the books on September
yet, but this is a typical month.

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:00.439
This is a August.

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:08.389
We got 40% of our revenue for memberships,
Patriot and apparel, 32.5% from YouTube ads,

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:12.430
22% from ad sales, three and a half percent
from Twitch.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.800
As many of you know, we're new to Twitch.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.490
So that's a pretty small part of our revenue
right now.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:21.340
Facebook ads, we're now monetizing on Facebook,
but only about 1% of our revenue and miscellaneous

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.219
donations are 0.1%.

00:06:23.219 --> 00:06:26.309
Now those miscellaneous donations of course
could come from anybody.

00:06:26.309 --> 00:06:29.529
Uh, but what I'm talking about is sometimes
people don't want a membership.

00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:31.969
They'll just send us, you know, a check for
a little bit of money.

00:06:31.969 --> 00:06:36.270
Uh, and that was 0.1% of our funding back
in August.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.219
We don't take money from any groups.

00:06:38.219 --> 00:06:41.419
If we have an advertiser, it's marked as an
advertisement.

00:06:41.419 --> 00:06:44.869
If we do a sponsored video, it's marked as
a sponsored video.

00:06:44.869 --> 00:06:45.869
That's it.

00:06:45.869 --> 00:06:49.430
So I can't speak to the strategy behind other
people's actions.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:54.629
I have no idea what people's financial situations
are and what would cause them to accept or

00:06:54.629 --> 00:06:57.039
not accept money from an organization like
this.

00:06:57.039 --> 00:06:59.120
Everybody's financial situations are different.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:05.849
And also, I don't know if what people are
concerned about is that the content of these

00:07:05.849 --> 00:07:11.059
programs is influenced by the fact that they've
received money from this group or if people

00:07:11.059 --> 00:07:14.180
are concerned about the lack of disclosure
or something else.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:20.659
And it would be interesting to clarify that,
but T to be very clear, um, people are often

00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:24.240
chosen for awards because they're saying the
right things.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.849
And of course the award can be a way to funnel
money to someone under the guise of we are

00:07:28.849 --> 00:07:32.349
rewarding you for good reporting or whatever
the case may be.

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:33.800
But typically that's not how it works.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.050
People, people are brought in, uh, or supported
because they're already saying the things

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.529
that the funder wants them to say.

00:07:39.529 --> 00:07:40.749
So that's our funding.

00:07:40.749 --> 00:07:44.639
I can't speak for anybody else and I hope
that this will sort of put to bed the questions

00:07:44.639 --> 00:07:45.189
I've been getting over the last a half day
or so.

